help[3]: "Fields per paper: id,title,url,category,class,tags,authors,year,arxiv,note",tags are space-separated; class is the primary arXiv class; authors are joined by ' and ',"Run `python scripts/papers.py` for a compact view, `python scripts/papers.py view <id>` for one paper"
papers[2526]{id,title,url,category,class,tags,authors,year,arxiv,note}:
  1,Ravi Vakil on Mathematical Writing,"https://math.stanford.edu/~vakil/greatwriting.html",stanford.edu,math.HO,math.HO mathematics mathematical-writing-and-practice,null,null,null,"Ravi Vakil on Mathematical Writing. Advice, reflections, and guidance on writing clearly and effectively in mathematics."
  2,Adelic and Classical Modular Forms for GL(2),"https://math.uchicago.edu/~emerton/gl2.pdf",uchicago.edu,math.NT,math.NT math.RT mathematics adeles modular-forms lie-theory complex-geometry automorphic-forms survey,null,null,null,"Adelic and Classical Modular Forms for GL(2). An exposition of the translation between classical modular forms and automorphic forms on the adelic group $\\mathrm{GL}_2(\\mathbb{A}_{\\mathbb{Q}})$. Provides a geometric interpretation of modular forms as sections of line bundles over modular curves, along with minimal ad hoc constructions of Eisenstein series. Details the Lie algebra $\\mathfrak{gl}_2(\\mathbb{R})$ with basis elements $Z, H, Y_+, Y_-$, where the center $\\mathcal{Z}(\\mathfrak{gl}_2)$ of the universal enveloping algebra is isomorphic to a polynomial ring in two generators. Explores the space of bases $B$ of $\\mathbb{C}$ as a real vector space, identifying it as an open subset of $\\mathbb{C}^2$ with commuting left and right actions by $\\mathrm{GL}_2(\\mathbb{R})$ and $\\mathrm{GL}_1(\\mathbb{C})$. The right action of $\\mathrm{GL}_2(\\mathbb{R})$ is complex analytic and gives an identification with the upper half-plane $\\mathcal{H}^{\\pm} \\times \\mathbb{C}^\\times$ via $(\\tau, z) \\mapsto \\left(\\frac{a\\tau+c}{b\\tau+d}, (b\\tau+d)z\\right)$. Examines the complexified Lie algebra tangent space decomposition into holomorphic and anti-holomorphic subspaces, the subspace $V_i \\subset \\mathfrak{gl}_2$, and the bijection $B/\\mathrm{GL}_2(\\mathbb{Z}) \\cong \\mathcal{L}$ with the moduli of discrete rank-2 lattices. Covers moderate growth conditions, smooth adelic automorphic forms, and representations invariant under right translation by $\\mathrm{GL}_2(\\mathbb{A}_f)$."
  3,Deligne on Modular Forms,"https://publications.ias.edu/sites/default/files/5_FormesModulaires.pdf",ias.edu,math.NT,math.NT mathematics modular-forms,null,null,null,"Deligne on Modular Forms. Foundational notes by Pierre Deligne on the algebraic and geometric theory of modular forms, referenced in Emerton's notes."
  4,Alex Youcis,"https://ayoucis.wordpress.com/2015/09/17/shimura-varieties-motivation/",wordpress.com,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics algebraic-geometry shimura-varieties blog,null,null,null,"Alex Youcis, Motivation behind Shimura Varieties. This will be the first in a series of posts discussing Shimura varieties. In particular, we will focus here on a sort of broad motivation for the subject—why Shimura varieties are a natural thing to study and, in particular, what they give us."
  5,Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Duality,"https://www.intlpress.com/site/pub/files/_fulltext/journals/cdm/1997/1997/0001/CDM-1997-1997-0001-a001.pdf",intlpress.com,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics algebraic-geometry galois-cohomology adeles etale-cohomology,null,null,null,"Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Duality. Connects the eigenvalues of the Frobenius action on étale cohomology $H_{\\text{ét}}^*(X, \\mathbb{Q}_\\ell)$ to the zeros and poles of zeta functions, completing the arithmetic dictionary via the adèle class space."
  6,Class Field Theory and Noncommutative Geometry,"https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/10843/contributions/12868/",cnrs.fr,math.NT,math.NT math.OA mathematics class-field-theory noncommutative-geometry adeles algebraic-number-theory survey,null,null,null,"Class Field Theory and Noncommutative Geometry. An exposition by Alain Connes on class field theory through the lens of the adèle class space $X_{\\mathbb{Q}} = \\mathbb{Q}^\\times \\backslash \\mathbb{A}_{\\mathbb{Q}}$. Abelian extensions of a number field $K$ are encoded internally by its idele class group $C_K = \\mathbb{A}_K^\\times / K^\\times$, acting as a Galois group of the maximal abelian extension via Artin reciprocity. Galois actions on roots are realized through group actions on spaces. The quotient space $X_K = K^\\times \\backslash \\mathbb{A}_K$ is ergodic with respect to the Haar measure, serving as a prototype noncommutative space (leaf space of a foliation). Translates local-to-global class field theory via the inclusion of local isotropy groups $K_v^\\times \\hookrightarrow C_K$. Connects the Riemann–Weil explicit formulas $\\sum_v \\int f(u)/|1-u|\\,d^*u$ to a trace formula for the scaling operator on the adèle class space. Introduces the scaling site $X_{\\mathbb{Q}} = \\mathbb{Q}^\\times \\backslash \\mathbb{A}_{\\mathbb{Q}} / \\widehat{\\mathbb{Z}}^\\times$, modeled as a noncommutative space of rank-1 subgroups of $\\mathbb{R}$, where periodic orbits of length $\\log p$ correspond to prime numbers $p$, realizing the Frobenius endomorphism as a mapping torus. Relates this construction to Grothendieck's étale fundamental group $\\pi_1^{\\text{ét}}$ and the 3D topology of $\\operatorname{Spec} \\mathbb{Z}$."
  7,Overview of O-Minimality,"https://math.berkeley.edu/~scanlon/papers/O-min-midrasha.pdf",berkeley.edu,math.LO,math.LO math.AG mathematics model-theory-in-geometry arithmetic-geometry mathematical-logic survey,null,null,null,"Overview of O-Minimality. Scanlon's survey on o-minimal structures, tame topology, and their applications in model theory and arithmetic geometry."
  8,Maximal Abelian Extensions Unramified Outside S,"https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/1897078/maximal-abelian-extension-unramified-outside-a-set-of-primes",stackexchange.com,math.NT,math.NT mathematics class-field-theory algebraic-number-theory distributed-systems galois-cohomology q-and-a stackexchange,null,null,null,"Maximal Abelian Extensions Unramified Outside S. Discussion and computation of the maximal abelian extension $K_S^{\\text{ab}}$ of a number field $K$ unramified outside a finite set of places $S$. For a singleton prime $S = \\{p\\}$, $K_S^{\\text{ab}}$ is given by the direct limit of ray class fields modulo $\\mathfrak{p}^n \\mathcal{O}_K$. Explains ramification at infinite places and the Galois group $G_S(K)^{\\text{ab}} = G_S(K) / \\overline{[G_S(K), G_S(K)]}$. Details the connection to class field theory, Poitou–Tate duality, and the Kronecker–Weber theorem for $K = \\mathbb{Q}$."
  9,Direct Proof of the Kronecker-Weber Theorem,"https://kskedlaya.org/18.786/ps10.pdf",kskedlaya.org,math.NT,math.NT mathematics class-field-theory cyclotomic-fields,null,null,null,"Direct Proof of the Kronecker-Weber Theorem. Lemmermeyer's direct proof showing that every finite abelian extension of $\\mathbb{Q}$ is contained in a cyclotomic field $\\mathbb{Q}(\\zeta_m)$."
  10,Ergodicity of Global Fields on Adeles,"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1211.3256",arxiv.org,math.DS,math.DS math.NT math.CA mathematics adeles ergodic-theory ode-and-dynamical-systems algebraic-number-theory arxiv,null,null,"1211.3256","Ergodicity of Global Fields on Adeles. Rigorous proof of the ergodicity of the action of $K^\\times$ on the adèle ring $\\mathbb{A}_K$ for global fields in both the number field and function field settings."
  11,Perspectives on Reciprocity Laws,"https://www.math.uchicago.edu/~emerton/pdffiles/reciprocity.pdf",uchicago.edu,math.NT,math.NT mathematics class-field-theory algebraic-number-theory langlands-program automorphic-forms survey,null,null,null,"Perspectives on Reciprocity Laws. Emerton's survey on reciprocity from Gauss's quadratic reciprocity to Langlands functoriality. Compares Dirichlet's analytic class number formula for $L(1, \\chi)$ (automorphic side) with Dedekind's class number formula (motivic side) and discusses the Sato–Tate conjecture."
  12,Categorical p-Adic Langlands Correspondence,"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2210.01404",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.CT math.RT mathematics category-theory langlands-program p-adic-langlands algebraic-geometry book arxiv,null,null,"2210.01404",Categorical p-Adic Langlands Correspondence. Comprehensive 252-page treatise by Emerton and Helm formulating the categorical $p$-adic Langlands program in both Banach and rigid analytic settings.
  13,Reductive Group Schemes after SGA3,"https://math.stanford.edu/~conrad/papers/luminysga3.pdf",stanford.edu,math.AG,math.AG mathematics algebraic-groups algebraic-geometry schemes lecture-notes historical-paper,null,null,null,Reductive Group Schemes after SGA3. Brian Conrad's foundational notes on the theory and classification of reductive group schemes over general bases.
  14,Research Remarks by Matthew Emerton,"https://math.uchicago.edu/~emerton/research.html",uchicago.edu,math.NT,math.NT math.RT mathematics automorphic-forms galois-representations langlands-program,null,null,null,"Research Remarks by Matthew Emerton. Collection of notes, papers, and essays by Matthew Emerton on automorphic forms, Galois representations, and the Langlands program."
  15,Fourier Analysis vs Representation Theory,"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/37021/is-fourier-analysis-a-special-case-of-representation-theory-or-an-analogue/37189#37189",mathoverflow.net,math.CA,math.CA math.RT mathematics harmonic-analysis representation-theory mathoverflow,null,null,null,"Fourier Analysis vs Representation Theory. Discussion on the relationship between harmonic analysis and group representations. Highlights the Peter–Weyl theorem for compact groups $G$, decomposing $L^2(G) \\cong \\widehat{\\bigoplus}_{\\pi} V_\\pi \\otimes V_\\pi^*$, and the Plancherel decomposition for non-compact type I groups via Harish-Chandra's work."
  16,Harmonic Analysis and Physics,"https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/58515/what-is-fourier-analysis-on-groups-and-does-it-have-applications-to-physics/58591#58591",stackexchange.com,math-ph,math-ph math.CA hep-th math.RT physics mathematics harmonic-analysis mathematical-physics lie-theory representation-theory survey stackexchange,null,null,null,"Harmonic Analysis and Physics. Survey of Plancherel decompositions on reductive Lie groups and Bargmann's classification of irreducible unitary representations of $\\mathrm{SL}_2(\\mathbb{R})$ with physical applications."
  17,Conceptual Meaning of the Weil Conjectures,"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/14849/what-would-a-moral-proof-of-the-weil-conjectures-require/14852#14852",mathoverflow.net,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics zeta-functions motives philosophy-of-mathematics mathoverflow,null,null,null,"Conceptual Meaning of the Weil Conjectures. Discussion on the philosophical and geometric requirements for proving the Weil conjectures via Weil cohomology theories, standard conjectures, and motives."
  18,Shimura's Problem and Class Field Theory,"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/10201/a-problem-of-shimura-and-its-relation-to-class-field-theory/10217#10217",mathoverflow.net,math.NT,math.NT mathematics class-field-theory cyclotomic-fields distributed-systems elliptic-curves mathoverflow,null,null,null,"Shimura's Problem and Class Field Theory. Explores the connection between polynomial splitting fields, ray class groups, and complex multiplication. Example: splitting of polynomials generating abelian extensions inside cyclotomic fields like $\\mathbb{Q}(\\zeta_7)$."
  19,Geometric Realization of Galois Representations,"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/62155/how-to-find-the-varieties-whose-cohomology-realizes-certain-representations/62211#62211",mathoverflow.net,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics galois-representations modular-forms algebraic-geometry etale-cohomology mathoverflow,null,null,null,"Geometric Realization of Galois Representations. Realizing 2-dimensional Galois representations attached to modular forms inside the étale cohomology $H^1_{\\text{ét}}(X_0(N)_{\\overline{\\mathbb{Q}}}, \\mathbb{Q}_\\ell)$ of modular curves, leading to Shimura varieties."
  20,The Moment Map and Equivariant Cohomology,"https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~mmovshev/MAT570Spring2008/BOOKS/atiyahbott_moment.pdf",stonybrook.edu,math.SG,math.SG math.AT math.AG mathematics symplectic-geometry equivariant-topology complex-geometry curves historical-paper,null,null,null,"The Moment Map and Equivariant Cohomology. Atiyah and Bott's foundational paper on the de Rham localization theorem in equivariant cohomology $H_G^*(M)$. Links Hamiltonian group actions, moment maps $\\mu: M \\to \\mathfrak{g}^*$, symplectic reduction, and the Duistermaat–Heckman exact stationary phase formula. Connects equivariant localization to moduli spaces of bundles on Riemann surfaces and Yang–Mills theory."
  21,Atiyah-Bott Localization in Geometry,"https://math.uchicago.edu/~may/REU2019/REUPapers/Lee%2CJaeHee.pdf",uchicago.edu,math.AT,math.AT mathematics equivariant-topology characteristic-classes survey,null,null,null,"Atiyah-Bott Localization in Geometry. Jae Hee Lee's expository REU paper detailing the Atiyah–Bott localization theorem, equivariant characteristic classes, and topological invariants of quotient manifolds."
  22,Moment Maps and Diffeomorphisms in Gauge Theory,"http://bogomolov-lab.ru/G-sem/AJM-3-1-001-016.pdf",bogomolov-lab.ru,hep-th,hep-th math.SG math-ph math.DG physics mathematics quantum-field-theory symplectic-geometry differential-geometry group-theory,null,null,null,"Moment Maps and Diffeomorphisms in Gauge Theory. Donaldson's paper interpreting the curvature of a connection on a surface principal bundle as a moment map for the gauge group action, applied to Yang–Mills equations."
  23,Convex Body Geometry by Keith Ball,"https://math.uchicago.edu/~shmuel/AAT-readings/Combinatorial%20Geometry%2C%20Concentration%2C%20Real%20Algebraic%20Geometry/ball.pdf",uchicago.edu,math.CO,math.CO math.FA math.MG math.OC mathematics convex-analysis discrete-geometry extremal-combinatorics functional-analysis survey,null,null,null,"Convex Body Geometry by Keith Ball. Comprehensive introduction to convex geometry, volume computation of Euclidean balls, the Hahn–Banach separation theorem, and extremal properties of polytopes and cubes."
  24,Non-Perturbative BV Theory via Derived Geometry,"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2307.15106",arxiv.org,hep-th,hep-th math-ph math.AG physics mathematics quantum-field-theory derived-algebraic-geometry diffeology-and-generalized-smooth-spaces differential-geometry arxiv,null,null,"2307.15106",Non-Perturbative BV Theory via Derived Geometry. Formulating non-perturbative Batalin–Vilkovisky (BV) quantization within derived differential geometry and shifted symplectic structures.
  25,Grothendieck's Tohoku Paper,"https://www.math.mcgill.ca/barr/papers/gk.pdf",mcgill.ca,math.CT,math.CT math.AG math.AT math.RA mathematics homological-algebra category-theory sheaf-cohomology sheaf-theory historical-paper,null,null,null,"Grothendieck's Tohoku Paper. Michael Barr's commentary on Grothendieck's landmark 1957 paper introducing abelian categories, derived functors $R^i F$, injective resolutions, sheaf cohomology, and the Grothendieck spectral sequence. Establishes the foundations for Serre duality and Ext functors of sheaves."
  26,Lectures on Serre's Modular Invariance Conjectures,"https://wstein.org/edu/Fall2003/252/references/ribet-stein-serre/ribet-stein.pdf",wstein.org,math.NT,math.NT mathematics galois-representations modular-forms lecture-notes survey,null,null,null,"Lectures on Serre's Modular Invariance Conjectures. Ribet and Stein's exposition on Serre's modularity conjecture linking odd, irreducible Galois representations $\\rho: \\operatorname{Gal}(\\overline{\\mathbb{Q}}/\\mathbb{Q}) \\to \\mathrm{GL}_2(\\mathbb{F}_p)$ to modular forms of specific weight and level."
  27,Injective Resolutions in Sheaf Cohomology,"https://mathoverflow.net/questions/1151/sheaf-cohomology-and-injective-resolutions",mathoverflow.net,math.AG,math.AG math.AT math.CT mathematics sheaf-cohomology homological-algebra sheaf-theory mathoverflow,null,null,null,"Injective Resolutions in Sheaf Cohomology. Comparison between computing sheaf cohomology using acyclic resolutions (e.g., flasque, soft, fine, or Čech on affine covers) and universal injective resolutions."
  28,Nilpotent Connections and Picard-Fuchs Equations,"https://www.numdam.org/item/10.1007/BF02684688.pdf",numdam.org,math.AT,math.AT math.DS math.CA mathematics chromatic-homotopy-theory ode-and-dynamical-systems historical-paper,null,null,null,"Nilpotent Connections and Picard-Fuchs Equations. Nick Katz's classic paper on regular singular differential equations, Gauss–Manin connections, and $p$-adic nilpotence."
  29,Serre's Faisceaux Algébriques Cohérents (FAC),"https://achinger.impan.pl/fac/fac.pdf",impan.pl,math.AG,math.AG math.AT mathematics algebraic-geometry sheaf-cohomology sheaf-theory historical-paper,null,null,null,"Serre's Faisceaux Algébriques Cohérents (FAC). Annotated translation of Serre's 1955 paper developing coherent sheaves $\\mathcal{O}_X$-modules and Čech cohomology on algebraic varieties under the Zariski topology."
  30,Transversality of a General Translate,"https://www.numdam.org/item/CM_1974__28_3_287_0.pdf",numdam.org,math.GT,math.GT math.DG math.AG mathematics differential-topology combinatorics enumerative-geometry perfectoid-spaces,null,null,null,Transversality of a General Translate. Kleiman's 12-page paper on the transversality of general translates in Schubert calculus and enumerative geometry over algebraically closed fields in characteristic zero.
  31,Introduction to Nonlinear PDEs,"https://web.math.princeton.edu/~seri/papers/gowers-Aug4-2006.pdf",princeton.edu,math.AP,math.AP mathematics pde survey,null,null,null,Introduction to Nonlinear PDEs. Sergiu Klainerman's comprehensive 72-page introduction to modern nonlinear wave equations and evolutionary PDEs.
  32,Brill-Noether Theory on K3 Surfaces,"https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/robert.lazarsfeld/Reprints/Lazarsfeld.BNP.pdf",stonybrook.edu,math.AG,math.AG mathematics algebraic-geometry,null,null,null,"Brill-Noether Theory on K3 Surfaces. Robert Lazarsfeld's 10-page proof of the Brill–Noether theorem and Gieseker's theorem using vector bundles on $K3$ surfaces with $\\operatorname{Pic}(X) \\cong \\mathbb{Z}$."
  33,Enumerative Geometry of Moduli Spaces of Curves,"https://www.dam.brown.edu/people/mumford/alg_geom/papers/1983b--EnumGeomModuli-NC.pdf",brown.edu,math.AG,math.AG math.CO mathematics moduli-spaces combinatorics enumerative-geometry intersection-theory,null,null,null,"Enumerative Geometry of Moduli Spaces of Curves. David Mumford's 58-page paper constructing the Chow ring $A^*(\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}_g)$ of the moduli space of stable curves, defining tautological classes $\\kappa_i, \\psi_i, \\lambda_i$, and applying Grothendieck–Riemann–Roch."
  34,Serre's GAGA Translation,"https://thomaskwaring.github.io/gaga.pdf",github.io,math.AG,math.AG math.AT mathematics sheaf-cohomology sheaf-theory algebraic-geometry complex-geometry github,null,null,null,Serre's GAGA Translation. English translation of Serre's 1956 paper Géométrie Algébrique et Géométrie Analytique establishing the equivalence between algebraic coherent sheaves and analytic coherent sheaves on projective complex varieties.
  35,Terence Tao's Harmonic Analysis Notes,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247a.1.06f/",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis lecture-notes,null,null,null,"Terence Tao's Harmonic Analysis Notes. Course materials covering Calderón–Zygmund theory, interpolation, singular integrals, and oscillatory integrals."
  36,Calderon-Zygmund-Stein Theory,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247a.1.06f/notes1.pdf",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis lecture-notes,null,null,null,"Calderon-Zygmund-Stein Theory. Tao's notes on classical Calderón–Zygmund theory, kernel estimates, and singular integral bounds on $L^p$ spaces."
  37,Complex and Real Interpolation,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247a.1.06f/notes2.pdf",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis survey,null,null,null,"Complex and Real Interpolation. Exposition of the Riesz–Thorin complex interpolation theorem, Marcinkiewicz real interpolation, and bounds on linear operators."
  38,Hardy-Littlewood Maximal Inequality,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247a.1.06f/notes3.pdf",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis,null,null,null,"Hardy-Littlewood Maximal Inequality. Detailed treatment of the Hardy–Littlewood maximal operator $Mf(x)$, weak $(1,1)$ bounds, and $L^p$ maximal inequalities."
  39,The Hilbert Transform,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247a.1.06f/notes4.pdf",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis,null,null,null,"The Hilbert Transform. Theory of the Hilbert transform, singular integral operators failing on the diagonal, and principal value integrals."
  40,Weighted Norm Inequalities,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247a.1.06f/notes5.pdf",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis,null,null,null,"Weighted Norm Inequalities. Muckenhoupt $A_p$ weights, weighted $L^p$ estimates, and boundedness of maximal operators."
  41,Introduction to Fourier Summation,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247a.1.06f/notes0.pdf",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis asymptotics-and-resummation real-analysis survey,null,null,null,Introduction to Fourier Summation. Motivating harmonic analysis through convergence of Fourier series and $L^p$ norm interpolation between extreme bounds.
  42,Paraproducts and Bilinear Operators,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/%7Etao/247b.1.07w/notes6.pdf",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis,null,null,null,"Paraproducts and Bilinear Operators. Analysis of multilinear operators, Coifman–Meyer paraproducts, and pointwise nonlinear estimates."
  43,The T(1) Theorem,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/%7Etao/247b.1.07w/notes7.pdf",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis,null,null,null,The T(1) Theorem. David and Journé's $T(1)$ theorem for $L^2$-boundedness of non-convolution Calderón–Zygmund operators via paraproducts and BMO estimates.
  44,Oscillatory Integrals,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/%7Etao/247b.1.07w/notes8.pdf",ucla.edu,math.ST,math.ST stat.ME mathematics statistics,null,null,null,"Oscillatory Integrals. Stationary phase methods, van der Corput lemma, and asymptotic estimation of oscillatory integrals."
  45,Harmonic Analysis on Finite Abelian Groups,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/%7Etao/247b.1.07w/notes9.pdf",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis group-theory,null,null,null,"Harmonic Analysis on Finite Abelian Groups. Discrete Fourier transforms, Pontryagin duality for finite groups, and convolution identities without measure-theoretic subtleties."
  46,Representation Theory of Finite Non-Abelian Groups,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/%7Etao/247b.1.07w/notes10.pdf",ucla.edu,math.RT,math.RT math.CA math.RA mathematics representation-theory harmonic-analysis linear-algebra,null,null,null,"Representation Theory of Finite Non-Abelian Groups. Noncommutative harmonic analysis, character theory, matrix coefficients, and Fourier inversion for finite non-abelian groups."
  47,Advanced Harmonic Analysis,"https://www.math.ucla.edu/~tao/247b.1.07w/",ucla.edu,math.CA,math.CA math.AP mathematics harmonic-analysis pde general-mathematics lecture-notes,null,null,null,"Advanced Harmonic Analysis. Course archive covering Littlewood–Paley theory, BMO spaces, and dispersive PDE techniques."
  48,Tate's Arithmetic of Elliptic Curves,"https://www.math.mcgill.ca/darmon/courses/16-17/mf/tate.pdf",mcgill.ca,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics elliptic-curves number-theory formal-groups lecture-notes,null,null,null,"Tate's Arithmetic of Elliptic Curves. Henri Darmon's notes based on Tate's classic lectures on elliptic curves, group laws, and formal groups."
  49,Number Theoretic Background for Tate's Thesis,"https://mathweb.ucsd.edu/~csorense/teaching/math205/Tate_Weil.pdf",ucsd.edu,math.NT,math.NT mathematics adeles number-theory harmonic-analysis riemann-zeta lecture-notes thesis,null,null,null,"Number Theoretic Background for Tate's Thesis. Claus Sorensen's notes on local fields, Haar measures, and Tate's Fourier-analytic reformulation of zeta functions."
