  59,The Six-Functor Formalism on Infinity-Categories,"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.26269",arxiv.org,math.CT,math.CT math.AG mathematics category-theory six-functor-formalism higher-category-theory formalization arxiv,null,null,"2510.26269","The Six-Functor Formalism on Infinity-Categories. Scholze's paper establishing the six-functor formalism as a lax symmetric monoidal functor from a category of correspondences $\\operatorname{Corr}(\\mathcal{C}, E)$ to $\\operatorname{Cat}_\\infty$. Formulates pushforward $f_*$, proper pushforward $f_!$, pullback $f^*$, exceptional pullback $f^!$, tensor product $\\otimes$, and internal $\\operatorname{\\mathcal{R}Hom}$. Deduces proper base change and the projection formula $f_!(A \\otimes f^*B) \\cong f_!(A) \\otimes B$ using Lurie's straightening/unstraightening for Cartesian fibrations over $\\operatorname{Fin}_*$. Discusses cohomological smoothness, local Verdier duality, and base change for rigid-analytic and perfectoid spaces."
