  96,Foundations of Six-Functor Formalisms,"https://mgallauer.warwick.ac.uk/docs/m6ff.pdf",ac.uk,math.CT,math.CT math.AG cs.LO mathematics computer-science category-theory six-functor-formalism formalization algebraic-topology book,null,null,null,"Foundations of Six-Functor Formalisms. Martin Gallauer's monograph explaining the categorical framework of the six functors ($f^*, f_*, f_!, f^!, \\otimes, \\underline{\\operatorname{Hom}}$) on coefficient systems. Formulates Grothendieck duality, relative purity, proper and smooth base change, localization exact triangles, and $\\mathbb{A}^1$-homotopy invariance. Discusses constructible $\\ell$-adic sheaves, holonomic $\\mathcal{D}$-modules, and the categorical representation of homology and cohomology via the tensor unit $\\mathbf{1}$."
  97,Fourier-Mukai Transforms and Push-Pull Duality,"https://epub.uni-regensburg.de/31403/6/final.pdf",uni-regensburg.de,math.AG,math.AG math.CA math.CT mathematics derived-categories harmonic-analysis category-theory differential-geometry,null,null,null,"Fourier-Mukai Transforms and Push-Pull Duality. Derived push-pull integral transforms $\\Phi_{\\mathcal{P}}(\\mathcal{F}) = \\mathbf{R}q_*(\\mathcal{P} \\otimes^{\\mathbf{L}} p^*\\mathcal{F})$ between derived categories of coherent sheaves and their extensions to $T^n$-principal bundles."
