  111,Concise Introduction to Almost Ring Theory,"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BhattAlmostRing.pdf",ncatlab.org,math.AC,math.AC math.AG math.NT math.CT mathematics commutative-algebra category-theory arithmetic-geometry deformation-theory lecture-notes survey nlab,null,null,null,"Concise Introduction to Almost Ring Theory. Bhargav Bhatt's notes on Faltings' almost mathematics over a perfectoid field $K$. Studies the valuation ring $K^\\circ$ with idempotent maximal ideal $\\mathfrak{m} = \\mathfrak{m}^2$. The category of almost modules $K^{\\circ a}\\text{-}\\mathbf{Mod} = K^\\circ\\text{-}\\mathbf{Mod} / \\Sigma$ is obtained by localizing at the Serre subcategory $\\Sigma$ of $\\mathfrak{m}$-torsion modules. Covers almost flatness, almost projective modules, diagonal idempotents, almost étale morphisms, and deformation theory via the almost purity theorem."
