  2288,Von Neumann Algebra Automorphisms and Time-Thermodynamics Relation in General Covariant Quantum Theories,"https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9406019",arxiv.org,gr-qc,gr-qc math.OA physics mathematics operator-algebras noncommutative-geometry arxiv,null,null,gr-qc/9406019,"Connes and Rovelli formulate the thermal-time hypothesis. Section 2 distinguishes the state-dependent modular automorphism group from the canonical state-independent flow in $\\operatorname{Out}(M)$."
  2289,Some Entanglement Properties of Quantum Field Theory,"https://link.aps.org/accepted/10.1103/RevModPhys.90.045003",aps.org,quant-ph,quant-ph hep-th math-ph physics quantum-information quantum-field-theory,null,null,null,"Witten's accessible account of operator-algebraic entanglement. Section IV.B, equation (IV.35), computes finite-dimensional modular flow as $a\\mapsto\\rho^{is}a\\rho^{-is}$."
  2290,Structure of von Neumann Algebras of Type III,"https://www.imsc.res.in/~sunder/mtnotes.pdf",imsc.res.in,math.OA,math.OA mathematics operator-algebras linear-algebra lecture-notes,null,null,null,"Takesaki's master-class notes on type III structure and flow of weights. Pages 31--33 compute modular automorphisms of weighted $2\\times2$ and $3\\times3$ matrix blocks and their periods."
  2291,Basic Noncommutative Geometry,"https://www.math.uwo.ca/faculty/khalkhali/files/BNCG_1sted.pdf",uwo.ca,math.OA,math.OA math-ph math.QA math.CT mathematics physics noncommutative-geometry groupoids,null,null,null,"Khalkhali's introductory text. Examples 2.1.5 and 2.5.9 compute the irrational Kronecker foliation's transverse groupoid $\\mathbb{T}\\rtimes_\\theta\\mathbb{Z}$ and identify its algebra with the noncommutative torus $A_\\theta$."
  2292,Perfectoid Spaces,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.4914",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics p-adic-hodge-theory perfectoid-spaces singularities arxiv,Peter Scholze,2011,"1111.4914","Perfectoid Spaces. Introduces perfectoid fields and perfectoid spaces, proves the tilting equivalence between perfectoid spaces over $K$ and over its tilt $K^\\flat$ in characteristic $p$, and deduces the weight-monodromy conjecture for complete intersections."
  2293,p-Adic Hodge Theory for Rigid-Analytic Varieties,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1205.3463",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics algebraic-geometry hodge-theory p-adic-hodge-theory differential-geometry arxiv,Peter Scholze,2012,"1205.3463","p-Adic Hodge Theory for Rigid-Analytic Varieties. Develops the pro-étale site and the period sheaves $\\mathbb{B}_{\\mathrm{dR}}^+$ on rigid-analytic varieties, proving the de Rham comparison and degeneration of the Hodge–de Rham spectral sequence for proper smooth rigid spaces."
  2294,Étale Cohomology of Diamonds,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.07343",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics perfectoid-spaces etale-cohomology category-theory formalization arxiv,Peter Scholze,2017,"1709.07343",Étale Cohomology of Diamonds. Defines diamonds as quotients of perfectoid spaces by pro-étale equivalence relations and builds the six-functor formalism for étale cohomology of diamonds and small v-stacks.
  2295,Integral p-Adic Hodge Theory,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.03148",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics hodge-theory p-adic-hodge-theory differential-geometry etale-cohomology arxiv,Bhargav Bhatt and Matthew Morrow and Peter Scholze,2016,"1602.03148","Integral p-Adic Hodge Theory. Constructs the $A_{\\mathrm{inf}}$-cohomology of proper smooth formal schemes over $\\mathcal{O}_C$ interpolating étale, crystalline and de Rham cohomology, and bounds torsion in étale cohomology by torsion in de Rham cohomology."
  2296,Topological Hochschild Homology and Integral p-Adic Hodge Theory,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.03261",arxiv.org,math.AT,math.AT math.AG math.NT math.KT mathematics topological-hochschild-homology algebraic-topology p-adic-hodge-theory hodge-theory arxiv,Bhargav Bhatt and Matthew Morrow and Peter Scholze,2018,"1802.03261","Topological Hochschild Homology and Integral p-Adic Hodge Theory. Recovers $A_{\\mathrm{inf}}$-cohomology and crystalline cohomology from topological Hochschild and topological cyclic homology via the motivic filtration on $\\mathrm{THH}$, $\\mathrm{TC}^-$ and $\\mathrm{TP}$ of quasisyntomic rings."
  2297,Absolute Prismatic Cohomology,"https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.06120",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics prismatic-cohomology algebraic-geometry schemes stacks arxiv,Bhargav Bhatt and Jacob Lurie,2022,"2201.06120","Absolute Prismatic Cohomology. Studies the absolute prismatic cohomology of $p$-adic formal schemes via the Cartier–Witt stack $\\mathrm{WCart}$, proving comparisons with syntomic cohomology and constructing prismatic F-gauges."
  2298,The Prismatization of p-Adic Formal Schemes,"https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.06124",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG mathematics prismatic-cohomology algebraic-geometry schemes sheaf-cohomology arxiv,Bhargav Bhatt and Jacob Lurie,2022,"2201.06124","The Prismatization of p-Adic Formal Schemes. Constructs the prismatization $X^{\\Delta}$ of a bounded $p$-adic formal scheme as a stack over $\\mathrm{WCart}$ whose quasi-coherent cohomology recovers absolute prismatic cohomology."
  2299,Prismatization,"https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.04746",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics prismatic-cohomology p-adic-hodge-theory stacks k-theory arxiv,Vladimir Drinfeld,2020,"2005.04746","Prismatization. Geometrizes prismatic cohomology through the stacks $\\Sigma$, $\\Sigma'$ and $\\Sigma''$ built from Witt vectors, describing the Hodge–Tate divisor and the Breuil–Kisin twists stack-theoretically."
  2300,The Pro-Étale Topology for Schemes,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG mathematics algebraic-geometry etale-cohomology perfectoid-spaces schemes arxiv,Bhargav Bhatt and Peter Scholze,2013,"1309.1198","The Pro-Étale Topology for Schemes. Defines the pro-étale site of a scheme, shows it is locally weakly contractible and replete, and uses it to give a clean definition of $\\ell$-adic sheaves and the constructible derived category."
  2301,The arc-Topology,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.04725",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG mathematics algebraic-geometry schemes commutative-algebra descent-theory arxiv,Bhargav Bhatt and Akhil Mathew,2018,"1807.04725","The arc-Topology. Introduces the arc-topology on qcqs schemes, detected by rank-one valuation rings, and proves arc-descent for étale cohomology with torsion coefficients and for perfect schemes."
  2302,"Relative p-Adic Hodge Theory: Foundations","https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.0792",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics p-adic-hodge-theory hodge-theory abstract-algebra perfectoid-spaces arxiv,Kiran S. Kedlaya and Ruochuan Liu,2013,"1301.0792","Relative p-Adic Hodge Theory: Foundations. Develops relative $(\\varphi, \\Gamma)$-modules over adic spaces, perfectoid algebras and the correspondence between étale local systems and $\\varphi$-modules over relative Robba rings."
  2303,An Introduction to the Theory of p-Adic Representations,"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0210184",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics galois-representations p-adic-hodge-theory differential-geometry geometric-invariant-theory survey arxiv,Laurent Berger,2002,math/0210184,"An Introduction to the Theory of p-Adic Representations. Survey of Fontaine's rings $\\mathbf{B}_{\\mathrm{cris}}, \\mathbf{B}_{\\mathrm{st}}, \\mathbf{B}_{\\mathrm{dR}}$, $(\\varphi, \\Gamma)$-modules, and the proof that de Rham representations are potentially semistable."
  2304,Prismatic Dieudonné Theory,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.10525",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics abelian-varieties prismatic-cohomology arxiv,Johannes Anschütz and Arthur-César Le Bras,2019,"1907.10525","Prismatic Dieudonné Theory. Classifies $p$-divisible groups over quasi-syntomic rings by admissible prismatic Dieudonné crystals, generalizing crystalline Dieudonné theory."
  2305,Foundations for Almost Ring Theory,"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0201175",arxiv.org,math.AC,math.AC math.AG math.NT mathematics commutative-algebra arithmetic-geometry descent-theory etale-cohomology arxiv,Ofer Gabber and Lorenzo Ramero,2002,math/0201175,"Foundations for Almost Ring Theory. Systematic treatment of almost mathematics: almost modules, almost algebras, almost étale extensions and descent, as used in Faltings' approach to $p$-adic Hodge theory."
  2306,Algebraization and Tannaka Duality,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1404.7483",arxiv.org,math.CT,math.CT math.QA math.AG mathematics monoidal-categories algebraic-geometry commutative-algebra schemes arxiv,Bhargav Bhatt,2014,"1404.7483","Algebraization and Tannaka Duality. Proves that for affine $X$, maps $\\operatorname{Spf} A \\to X$ from complete noetherian rings algebraize, via a Tannaka duality for perfect complexes on qcqs schemes."
  2307,"Proof of the Geometric Langlands Conjecture I: Construction of the Functor","https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.03599",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.CT math.NT math.RT mathematics category-theory geometric-langlands langlands-program automorphic-forms arxiv,Dennis Gaitsgory and Sam Raskin,2024,"2405.03599","Proof of the Geometric Langlands Conjecture I: Construction of the Functor. Constructs the geometric Langlands functor from the automorphic category $\\mathrm{D\\text{-}mod}_{\\frac12}(\\mathrm{Bun}_G)$ to $\\mathrm{IndCoh}_{\\mathrm{Nilp}}(\\mathrm{LocSys}_{\\check G})$ and shows the de Rham, Betti, restricted and tempered forms of the conjecture are equivalent."
  2308,Periods and Harmonic Analysis on Spherical Varieties,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1203.0039",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT math.RT math.CA mathematics algebraic-geometry relative-langlands harmonic-analysis motives arxiv,Yiannis Sakellaridis and Akshay Venkatesh,2012,"1203.0039","Periods and Harmonic Analysis on Spherical Varieties. Develops Plancherel formulas for spherical varieties $X = H \\backslash G$ over local fields and formulates conjectures relating global $H$-periods to special values of L-functions determined by the dual group $\\check G_X$."
  2309,"Symplectic Local Root Numbers, Central Critical L-Values, and Restriction Problems","https://arxiv.org/abs/0909.2999",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.SG mathematics l-functions symplectic-geometry langlands-program group-theory arxiv,Wee Teck Gan and Benedict H. Gross and Dipendra Prasad,2009,"0909.2999","Symplectic Local Root Numbers, Central Critical L-Values, and Restriction Problems. States the Gan–Gross–Prasad conjectures on branching laws for classical groups in terms of symplectic root numbers of Langlands parameters, and their global analogue relating period integrals to central L-values."
  2310,Le Lemme Fondamental pour les Algèbres de Lie,"https://arxiv.org/abs/0801.0446",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.AT math.RT math.NT mathematics algebraic-topology perverse-sheaves langlands-program sheaf-theory arxiv,Bao Châu Ngô,2008,"0801.0446","Le Lemme Fondamental pour les Algèbres de Lie. Proves the fundamental lemma of Langlands–Shelstad using the cohomology of the Hitchin fibration, perverse sheaves, the decomposition theorem and a support theorem for abelian fibrations."
  2311,Chtoucas pour les Groupes Réductifs et Paramétrisation de Langlands Globale,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1209.5352",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.RT mathematics langlands-program algebraic-groups automorphic-forms function-fields arxiv,Vincent Lafforgue,2012,"1209.5352",Chtoucas pour les Groupes Réductifs et Paramétrisation de Langlands Globale. Constructs the automorphic-to-Galois direction of global Langlands for any reductive group over a function field using excursion operators on the cohomology of moduli of shtukas.
  2312,The Conjectural Connections Between Automorphic Representations and Galois Representations,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1009.0785",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.RT mathematics automorphic-forms galois-representations arxiv,Kevin Buzzard and Toby Gee,2010,"1009.0785",The Conjectural Connections Between Automorphic Representations and Galois Representations. Formulates $C$-algebraic and $L$-algebraic automorphic representations and states precise conjectures attaching Galois representations valued in the C-group to algebraic automorphic representations.
  2313,Modularity Lifting Beyond the Taylor–Wiles Method,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.4224",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT mathematics galois-representations arxiv,Frank Calegari and David Geraghty,2012,"1207.4224","Modularity Lifting Beyond the Taylor–Wiles Method. Extends Taylor–Wiles patching to settings where the defect $\\ell_0 > 0$, proving minimal modularity lifting for weight-one forms and, conditionally, for $\\mathrm{GL}_n$ over CM fields."
  2314,Potential Automorphy over CM Fields,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.09999",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT mathematics galois-representations curves elliptic-curves arxiv,Patrick B. Allen and Frank Calegari and Ana Caraiani and Toby Gee and David Helm and Bao V. Le Hung and James Newton and Peter Scholze and Richard Taylor and Jack A. Thorne,2018,"1812.09999",Potential Automorphy over CM Fields. Proves potential automorphy of elliptic curves over CM fields and the Ramanujan conjecture on average via local-global compatibility for torsion classes and a new Taylor–Wiles patching argument.
  2315,On the Rigid Cohomology of Certain Shimura Varieties,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.6717",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics algebraic-geometry shimura-varieties automorphic-forms galois-representations arxiv,Michael Harris and Kai-Wen Lan and Richard Taylor and Jack Thorne,2014,"1411.6717","On the Rigid Cohomology of Certain Shimura Varieties. Constructs Galois representations for regular algebraic cuspidal automorphic representations of $\\mathrm{GL}_n$ over CM fields via $p$-adic interpolation on unitary Shimura varieties."
  2316,An Introduction to Affine Grassmannians and the Geometric Satake Equivalence,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593",arxiv.org,math.RT,math.RT math.AG math.NT mathematics geometric-representation-theory algebraic-groups langlands-program algebraic-geometry lecture-notes survey arxiv,Xinwen Zhu,2016,"1603.05593","An Introduction to Affine Grassmannians and the Geometric Satake Equivalence. Lecture notes on affine Grassmannians, their Schubert varieties, the convolution product and the geometric Satake equivalence $\\mathrm{Perv}_{L^+G}(\\mathrm{Gr}_G) \\simeq \\mathrm{Rep}(\\check G)$, including mixed-characteristic versions."
  2317,Geometric Langlands Duality and Representations of Algebraic Groups over Commutative Rings,"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0401222",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.RT math.NT mathematics algebraic-groups langlands-program representation-theory geometric-langlands geometric-representation-theory arxiv,Ivan Mirković and Kari Vilonen,2004,math/0401222,"Geometric Langlands Duality and Representations of Algebraic Groups over Commutative Rings. Proves the geometric Satake equivalence with integral coefficients, identifying $L^+G$-equivariant perverse sheaves on the affine Grassmannian with representations of the dual group scheme over any commutative ring."
  2318,Electric-Magnetic Duality and the Geometric Langlands Program,"https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0604151",arxiv.org,hep-th,hep-th math.AG math.NT math.RT physics mathematics geometric-langlands langlands-program string-theory complex-geometry arxiv,Anton Kapustin and Edward Witten,2006,hep-th/0604151,"Electric-Magnetic Duality and the Geometric Langlands Program. Derives geometric Langlands from S-duality of topologically twisted $\\mathcal{N}=4$ super Yang–Mills theory compactified on a Riemann surface, with 't Hooft operators acting as Hecke operators on branes in the Hitchin moduli space."
  2319,Singular Support of Coherent Sheaves and the Geometric Langlands Conjecture,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6343",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.AP math.NT math.RT mathematics microlocal-analysis geometric-langlands langlands-program sheaf-theory derived-algebraic-geometry arxiv,Dima Arinkin and Dennis Gaitsgory,2012,"1201.6343",Singular Support of Coherent Sheaves and the Geometric Langlands Conjecture. Introduces singular support for ind-coherent sheaves on quasi-smooth derived stacks and uses it to formulate the corrected geometric Langlands conjecture with nilpotent singular support.
  2320,On Some Finiteness Questions for Algebraic Stacks,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1108.5351",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG mathematics stacks geometric-representation-theory arxiv,Vladimir Drinfeld and Dennis Gaitsgory,2011,"1108.5351","On Some Finiteness Questions for Algebraic Stacks. Proves compact generation of $\\mathrm{QCoh}$ and D-modules on QCA stacks, and that $\\mathrm{D\\text{-}mod}(\\mathrm{Bun}_G)$ is compactly generated via truncatable open substacks."
  2321,"The Motivic Fundamental Group of $\\mathbb{P}^1 \\setminus \\{0,1,\\infty\\}$ and the Theorem of Siegel","https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0409456",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.AT math.NT mathematics algebraic-topology motives arithmetic-geometry algebraic-geometry arxiv,Minhyong Kim,2004,math/0409456,"The Motivic Fundamental Group of $\\mathbb{P}^1 \\setminus \\{0,1,\\infty\\}$ and the Theorem of Siegel. Introduces unipotent Selmer varieties and a non-abelian Chabauty method, reproving Siegel's finiteness of integral points on $\\mathbb{P}^1 \\setminus \\{0,1,\\infty\\}$."
  2322,The Unipotent Albanese Map and Selmer Varieties for Curves,"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0510441",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics algebraic-geometry arithmetic-geometry arxiv,Minhyong Kim,2005,math/0510441,The Unipotent Albanese Map and Selmer Varieties for Curves. Develops the unipotent Albanese map from a curve to its Selmer varieties and gives conditions under which Chabauty–Kim proves finiteness of rational points.
  2323,Explicit Chabauty–Kim for the Split Cartan Modular Curve of Level 13,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.05846",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.RT math.AG mathematics arithmetic-geometry lie-theory modular-forms arxiv,Jennifer Balakrishnan and Netan Dogra and J. Steffen Müller and Jan Tuitman and Jan Vonk,2017,"1711.05846","Explicit Chabauty–Kim for the Split Cartan Modular Curve of Level 13. Uses quadratic Chabauty to determine the rational points of the genus-3 modular curve $X_s(13)$, completing the classification of split Cartan images mod 13."
  2324,Diophantine Problems and p-Adic Period Mappings,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.02721",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics hodge-theory number-theory arithmetic-geometry singularities arxiv,Brian Lawrence and Akshay Venkatesh,2018,"1807.02721",Diophantine Problems and p-Adic Period Mappings. Proves finiteness of $S$-integral points on hypersurfaces and reproves Mordell's conjecture using big monodromy of variations of Hodge structure and $p$-adic period maps.
  2325,"Binary Quartic Forms Having Bounded Invariants, and the Boundedness of the Average Rank of Elliptic Curves","https://arxiv.org/abs/1006.1002",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics elliptic-curves quadratic-forms curves arxiv,Manjul Bhargava and Arul Shankar,2010,"1006.1002","Binary Quartic Forms Having Bounded Invariants, and the Boundedness of the Average Rank of Elliptic Curves. Counts $\\mathrm{PGL}_2(\\mathbb{Z})$-orbits of binary quartic forms to show the average size of the 2-Selmer group of elliptic curves over $\\mathbb{Q}$ is 3, bounding the average rank by 1.5."
  2326,"Ternary Cubic Forms Having Bounded Invariants, and the Existence of a Positive Proportion of Elliptic Curves Having Rank 0","https://arxiv.org/abs/1007.0052",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics elliptic-curves quadratic-forms arxiv,Manjul Bhargava and Arul Shankar,2010,"1007.0052","Ternary Cubic Forms Having Bounded Invariants, and the Existence of a Positive Proportion of Elliptic Curves Having Rank 0. Computes the average size of 3-Selmer groups as 4 and deduces that the average rank is below 1.17 and a positive proportion of elliptic curves have rank 0."
  2327,Random Maximal Isotropic Subspaces and Selmer Groups,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1009.0317",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics elliptic-curves arithmetic-statistics functional-analysis arxiv,Bjorn Poonen and Eric Rains,2010,"1009.0317","Random Maximal Isotropic Subspaces and Selmer Groups. Models $p$-Selmer groups as intersections of random maximal isotropic subspaces in a quadratic space, predicting the distribution of Selmer ranks."
  2328,"Modeling the Distribution of Ranks, Selmer Groups, and Shafarevich–Tate Groups of Elliptic Curves","https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.3971",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.AG math.FA mathematics elliptic-curves arithmetic-statistics functional-analysis linear-algebra arxiv,Manjul Bhargava and Daniel M. Kane and Hendrik W. Lenstra Jr. and Bjorn Poonen and Eric Rains,2013,"1304.3971","Modeling the Distribution of Ranks, Selmer Groups, and Shafarevich–Tate Groups of Elliptic Curves. Models Selmer and Shafarevich–Tate groups by cokernels of random alternating matrices, giving a unified heuristic consistent with Cohen–Lenstra and Poonen–Rains."
  2329,Homological Stability for Hurwitz Spaces and the Cohen–Lenstra Conjecture over Function Fields,"https://arxiv.org/abs/0912.0325",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.AT math.AG math.GT mathematics arithmetic-statistics function-fields homological-stability arxiv,Jordan S. Ellenberg and Akshay Venkatesh and Craig Westerland,2009,"0912.0325","Homological Stability for Hurwitz Spaces and the Cohen–Lenstra Conjecture over Function Fields. Proves homological stability for Hurwitz spaces of branched covers and deduces the Cohen–Lenstra heuristics for $\\mathbb{F}_q(t)$ in the large-$q$ limit."
  2330,"The André–Oort Conjecture for $\\mathcal{A}_g$","https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01466",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.NT mathematics shimura-varieties abelian-varieties algebraic-geometry model-theory-in-geometry arxiv,Jacob Tsimerman,2015,"1506.01466","The André–Oort Conjecture for $\\mathcal{A}_g$. Completes the proof of André–Oort for the moduli of principally polarized abelian varieties by combining the averaged Colmez conjecture with the Pila–Zannier o-minimal strategy."
  2331,Tame Topology of Arithmetic Quotients and Algebraicity of Hodge Loci,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.04801",arxiv.org,math.LO,math.LO math.AG mathematics model-theory-in-geometry hodge-theory arxiv,Benjamin Bakker and Bruno Klingler and Jacob Tsimerman,2018,"1810.04801","Tame Topology of Arithmetic Quotients and Algebraicity of Hodge Loci. Shows period maps are definable in $\\mathbb{R}_{\\mathrm{an,exp}}$ and gives an o-minimal proof of the Cattani–Deligne–Kaplan algebraicity of Hodge loci."
  2332,o-Minimal GAGA and a Conjecture of Griffiths,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.12230",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.LO math.AT mathematics sheaf-cohomology model-theory-in-geometry algebraic-geometry hodge-theory arxiv,Benjamin Bakker and Yohan Brunebarbe and Jacob Tsimerman,2018,"1811.12230",o-Minimal GAGA and a Conjecture of Griffiths. Proves a GAGA theorem for definable analytic spaces and deduces that images of period maps are quasi-projective algebraic varieties.
  2333,Geometry of the Scaling Site,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.05818",arxiv.org,math.AG,math.AG math.CT math.LO math.NT mathematics field-with-one-element topos-theory intersection-theory tropical-geometry arxiv,Alain Connes and Caterina Consani,2015,"1507.05818","Geometry of the Scaling Site. Studies the scaling site obtained from the arithmetic site by extension of scalars, its points as a tropical curve-like space and the Riemann–Roch problem for its periodic orbits."
  2334,Trace Formula in Noncommutative Geometry and the Zeros of the Riemann Zeta Function,"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9811068",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT mathematics riemann-zeta automorphic-forms zeta-functions noncommutative-geometry arxiv,Alain Connes,1998,math/9811068,"Trace Formula in Noncommutative Geometry and the Zeros of the Riemann Zeta Function. Proposes a spectral realization of the zeros of the zeta function via the action of the idele class group on the adèle class space, reducing RH to a trace formula (the Weil positivity)."
  2335,From Physics to Number Theory via Noncommutative Geometry,"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404128",arxiv.org,math.OA,math.OA math-ph math.NT math.QA mathematics physics noncommutative-geometry mathematical-physics number-theory operator-algebras survey arxiv,Alain Connes and Matilde Marcolli,2004,math/0404128,"From Physics to Number Theory via Noncommutative Geometry. Survey of quantum statistical mechanics of $\\mathbb{Q}$-lattices, the Bost–Connes and GL$_2$ systems, KMS states and their arithmetic symmetries."
  2336,An Essay on the Riemann Hypothesis,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.05576",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT mathematics riemann-zeta adeles field-with-one-element function-fields survey arxiv,Alain Connes,2015,"1509.05576","An Essay on the Riemann Hypothesis. Surveys approaches to RH through Weil's proof over function fields, the adèle class space, the arithmetic site and the search for a geometry underlying the explicit formulas."
  2337,"Weil Positivity and Trace Formula, the Archimedean Place","https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.13771",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.RT mathematics automorphic-forms arxiv,Alain Connes and Caterina Consani,2020,"2006.13771","Weil Positivity and Trace Formula, the Archimedean Place. Proves Weil positivity for test functions supported in a small interval at the archimedean place, using prolate spheroidal wave functions and the semilocal trace formula."
  2338,The Primes Contain Arbitrarily Long Arithmetic Progressions,"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404188",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.CO mathematics additive-combinatorics number-theory complexity-theory arxiv,Ben Green and Terence Tao,2004,math/0404188,"The Primes Contain Arbitrarily Long Arithmetic Progressions. Proves the Green–Tao theorem through a transference principle: a relative Szemerédi theorem for pseudorandom majorants applied to the Goldston–Yıldırım weights."
  2339,Small Gaps Between Primes,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.4600",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT mathematics number-theory analytic-number-theory real-analysis arxiv,James Maynard,2013,"1311.4600","Small Gaps Between Primes. Introduces multidimensional Selberg sieve weights, showing $\\liminf (p_{n+m} - p_n) \\ll m^3 e^{4m}$ and bounded gaps at most 600."
  2340,New Large Value Estimates for Dirichlet Polynomials,"https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.20552",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT mathematics analytic-number-theory number-theory arxiv,Larry Guth and James Maynard,2024,"2405.20552","New Large Value Estimates for Dirichlet Polynomials. Improves Ingham's zero-density estimate to $N(\\sigma, T) \\le T^{30(1-\\sigma)/13 + o(1)}$ by bounding large values of Dirichlet polynomials near $N^{3/4}$, with applications to primes in short intervals."
  2341,Moments of the Riemann Zeta Function,"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0612106",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics riemann-zeta zeta-functions arxiv,Kannan Soundararajan,2006,math/0612106,"Moments of the Riemann Zeta Function. Proves on RH the almost sharp upper bound $\\int_0^T |\\zeta(\\tfrac12 + it)|^{2k} dt \\ll T (\\log T)^{k^2 + \\varepsilon}$."
  2342,Sharp Conditional Bounds for Moments of the Riemann Zeta Function,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1305.4618",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.AG mathematics riemann-zeta zeta-functions arxiv,Adam J. Harper,2013,"1305.4618","Sharp Conditional Bounds for Moments of the Riemann Zeta Function. Removes the $\\varepsilon$ in Soundararajan's bound, proving on RH the sharp order $T (\\log T)^{k^2}$ for all moments."
  2343,Proof of the Main Conjecture in Vinogradov's Mean Value Theorem for Degrees Higher Than Three,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.01565",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT mathematics iwasawa-theory analytic-number-theory harmonic-analysis arxiv,Jean Bourgain and Ciprian Demeter and Larry Guth,2015,"1512.01565","Proof of the Main Conjecture in Vinogradov's Mean Value Theorem for Degrees Higher Than Three. Proves the Vinogradov main conjecture via $\\ell^2$ decoupling for the moment curve, a harmonic-analysis approach to exponential sums."
  2344,"The Proof of the $\\ell^2$ Decoupling Conjecture","https://arxiv.org/abs/1403.5335",arxiv.org,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis arxiv,Jean Bourgain and Ciprian Demeter,2014,"1403.5335","The Proof of the $\\ell^2$ Decoupling Conjecture. Proves sharp $\\ell^2$ decoupling for compact hypersurfaces with positive definite second fundamental form, with applications to Strichartz estimates and lattice point counting."
  2345,A Restriction Estimate Using Polynomial Partitioning,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1407.1916",arxiv.org,math.CA,math.CA mathematics harmonic-analysis networking arxiv,Larry Guth,2014,"1407.1916","A Restriction Estimate Using Polynomial Partitioning. Proves new Fourier restriction estimates in $\\mathbb{R}^3$ via polynomial partitioning, controlling wave packets concentrated near algebraic surfaces."
  2346,Strong Bounds for 3-Progressions,"https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.05537",arxiv.org,math.GM,math.GM mathematics arxiv,Zander Kelley and Raghu Meka,2023,"2302.05537","Strong Bounds for 3-Progressions. Shows subsets of $\\{1, \\dots, N\\}$ free of 3-term progressions have density $\\exp(-c (\\log N)^{1/12})$, using almost-periodicity and a new density-increment on spectral sets."
  2347,Breaking the Logarithmic Barrier in Roth's Theorem on Arithmetic Progressions,"https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.03528",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO math.NT mathematics additive-combinatorics arxiv,Thomas F. Bloom and Olof Sisask,2020,"2007.03528","Breaking the Logarithmic Barrier in Roth's Theorem on Arithmetic Progressions. Improves Roth's theorem to density $(\\log N)^{-1-c}$, answering an Erdős conjecture for 3-term progressions."
  2348,On a Conjecture of Marton,"https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.05762",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO math.NT cs.IT mathematics computer-science additive-combinatorics information-theory arxiv,W. T. Gowers and Ben Green and Freddie Manners and Terence Tao,2023,"2311.05762","On a Conjecture of Marton. Proves the polynomial Freiman–Ruzsa conjecture over $\\mathbb{F}_2^n$ using an entropic formulation and the entropic Ruzsa distance."
  2349,Szemerédi's Regularity Lemma Revisited,"https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0504472",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO mathematics extremal-combinatorics additive-combinatorics probability arxiv,Terence Tao,2005,math/0504472,"Szemerédi's Regularity Lemma Revisited. Recasts the regularity lemma as an energy-increment argument in probability spaces, yielding the removal lemma and a proof of Roth's theorem."
  2350,Structure and Randomness in Combinatorics,"https://arxiv.org/abs/0707.4269",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO mathematics combinatorics additive-combinatorics complexity-theory extremal-combinatorics arxiv,Terence Tao,2007,"0707.4269","Structure and Randomness in Combinatorics. FOCS tutorial on the dichotomy between structure and pseudorandomness via regularity lemmas, Gowers norms and the transference principle."
  2351,"The Dichotomy Between Structure and Randomness, Arithmetic Progressions, and the Primes","https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0512114",arxiv.org,math.NT,math.NT math.CO mathematics additive-combinatorics number-theory complexity-theory arxiv,Terence Tao,2005,math/0512114,"The Dichotomy Between Structure and Randomness, Arithmetic Progressions, and the Primes. ICM lecture explaining how structure theorems decomposing objects into structured and pseudorandom parts underlie Szemerédi's theorem and Green–Tao."
  2352,"Convergent Sequences of Dense Graphs I: Subgraph Frequencies, Metric Properties and Testing","https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0702004",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO cs.SE math.CA mathematics computer-science software-engineering extremal-combinatorics graph-theory real-analysis arxiv,Christian Borgs and Jennifer Chayes and László Lovász and Vera T. Sós and Katalin Vesztergombi,2007,math/0702004,"Convergent Sequences of Dense Graphs I: Subgraph Frequencies, Metric Properties and Testing. Proves equivalence of left convergence and convergence in cut distance, and applies it to property testing."
