  2354,An Exponential Improvement for Diagonal Ramsey,"https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.09521",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO mathematics extremal-combinatorics graph-theory algorithms book arxiv,Marcelo Campos and Simon Griffiths and Robert Morris and Julian Sahasrabudhe,2023,"2303.09521","An Exponential Improvement for Diagonal Ramsey. Proves $R(k) \\le (4 - \\varepsilon)^k$ with a book-algorithm that finds large red books or blue cliques."
  2355,A Proof of the Kahn–Kalai Conjecture,"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.17207",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO math.PR mathematics probabilistic-combinatorics arxiv,Jinyoung Park and Huy Tuan Pham,2022,"2203.17207",A Proof of the Kahn–Kalai Conjecture. Shows the threshold of any monotone property is within a logarithmic factor of its expectation threshold.
  2356,Improved Bounds for the Sunflower Lemma,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.08483",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO mathematics extremal-combinatorics arxiv,Ryan Alweiss and Shachar Lovett and Kewen Wu and Jiapeng Zhang,2019,"1908.08483","Improved Bounds for the Sunflower Lemma. Improves the Erdős–Rado sunflower bound to $(\\log k \\cdot \\log\\log k)^{k}$ via spread families and the robust sunflower lemma."
  2357,Milnor Numbers of Projective Hypersurfaces and the Chromatic Polynomial of Graphs,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1008.4749",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO math.AT mathematics graph-theory algebraic-combinatorics chromatic-homotopy-theory arxiv,June Huh,2010,"1008.4749",Milnor Numbers of Projective Hypersurfaces and the Chromatic Polynomial of Graphs. Proves log-concavity of the coefficients of the chromatic polynomial (Read's conjecture) by identifying them with mixed multiplicities of a hyperplane arrangement.
  2358,Lorentzian Polynomials,"https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.03719",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO math.RT mathematics algebraic-combinatorics arxiv,Petter Brändén and June Huh,2019,"1902.03719","Lorentzian Polynomials. Defines Lorentzian polynomials generalizing volume polynomials and stable polynomials, proving ultra log-concavity for independent sets of matroids (Mason's conjecture)."
  2359,"Log-Concave Polynomials II: High-Dimensional Walks and an FPRAS for Counting Bases of a Matroid","https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.01816",arxiv.org,math.CO,math.CO math.RT mathematics algebraic-combinatorics arxiv,Nima Anari and Kuikui Liu and Shayan Oveis Gharan and Cynthia Vinzant,2018,"1811.01816","Log-Concave Polynomials II: High-Dimensional Walks and an FPRAS for Counting Bases of a Matroid. Proves the bases-exchange walk on any matroid mixes rapidly via log-concavity of the basis generating polynomial."
